# ============================================================================
# SECURITY NOTES
# ============================================================================

# Token Storage:
# - Access tokens: Store in memory or short-lived httpOnly cookies
# - Refresh tokens: Store in httpOnly cookies with secure flag
# - Never store tokens in localStorage (vulnerable to XSS)

# Token Transmission:
# - Always use HTTPS in production
# - Use Authorization: Bearer <token> header
# - Never send tokens in URL parameters

# Token Lifecycle:
# 1. User authenticates -> Receive access + refresh tokens
# 2. Use access token for API requests
# 3. When access token expires -> Use refresh token to get new access token
# 4. When refresh token expires -> User must re-authenticate
# 5. On logout -> Revoke both tokens

# Token Claims:
# Required claims:
# - sub: User ID
# - iat: Issued at timestamp
# - exp: Expiration timestamp
# - iss: Issuer
# - aud: Audience
#
# Optional claims:
# - email: User email
# - roles: User roles array
# - permissions: User permissions array
# - sessionId: Session identifier

# ============================================================================
# MONITORING AND ALERTS
# ============================================================================

# Monitor these metrics:
# - Token generation rate (detect brute force)
# - Token validation failures (detect tampering)
# - Refresh token usage (detect token theft)
# - Expired token attempts (normal, but monitor for abuse)
# - Revoked token attempts (potential security incident)

# Alert on:
# - High token validation failure rate
# - Unusual refresh token usage patterns
# - Multiple revoked token access attempts
# - Token generation from unusual IP addresses

# ============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ============================================================================

# Common Issues:

# 1. "Invalid token" errors:
#    - Verify JWT_ACCESS_SECRET matches between auth service and API gateway
#    - Check token expiration time
#    - Verify issuer and audience match

# 2. "Token expired" errors:
#    - Check system time synchronization
#    - Verify JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN is not too short
#    - Implement proper token refresh flow

# 3. "Invalid signature" errors:
#    - Ensure JWT_ACCESS_SECRET is consistent across services
#    - Check for secret rotation during token validity period
#    - Verify algorithm is HS256

# 4. Token refresh not working:
#    - Verify JWT_REFRESH_SECRET is set and different from access secret
#    - Check refresh token expiration
#    - Ensure refresh token rotation is properly implemented

